          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(II) Preparing a soda-acid fire extinguisher"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.119,
            0.868,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The reaction of acids with metal hydrogencarbonates is used in the fire extinguishers which produce carbon dioxide.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.155,
            0.848,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n Take 20 mL of sodium hydrogencarbonate "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{(NaHCO_{3})}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "solution in a wash-bottle.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.174,
            0.868,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suspend an ignition tube containing dilute sulphuric acid in the wash-bottle "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(Fig. 2.10).",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.211,
            0.471,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Close the mouth of the wash-bottle.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.23,
            0.868,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Tilt the wash-bottle so that the acid from the ignition tube mixes with the sodium "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "hydrogencarbonate solution below.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.266,
            0.6,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You will notice discharge coming out of the nozzle.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.286,
            0.671,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Direct this discharge on a burning candle. What happens?"
